@model ProductionLineAssignmentForm
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Production-line assignment";
}
<p><a href="/plants/@Model.PlantId">Back to plant</a></p>
<h1>Production-line assignment</h1>
<section class="panel">
    <p>Plant: <code>@Model.PlantId</code>. Binding version: @Model.ExpectedVersion.</p>
    <p>One configured line per plant in this slice. Assignment requires ownership of the plant and line.
        Active enrolled workbenches inherit the configuration; no individual line assignment is required.</p>
    <p><a href="/production-lines">Find or define a production line</a>, then copy its line ID below.</p>
    <form action="/plants/@Model.PlantId/production-line" method="post" asp-antiforgery="true">
        <div asp-validation-summary="All" role="alert"></div>
        <input type="hidden" asp-for="ExpectedVersion" />
        <label asp-for="ProductionLineId">Production-line ID (leave empty to revoke)</label>
        <input asp-for="ProductionLineId" />
        <p>Clearing or replacing the assignment revokes the old configuration for this plant's workbenches.
            Device unassignment/move also revokes that device's old configuration.
            In-flight work must be stopped, not gracefully drained; quiescing is a future capability.</p>
        <button class="button" type="submit">Save assignment</button>
    </form>
</section>
<section class="panel">
    <h2>Workbench acknowledgments</h2>
    <p>Each workbench reports its own applied configuration and blockers.
        <a href="/plants/@Model.PlantId/workbenches">View this plant's workbenches</a> to inspect their acknowledgments.</p>
    <p class="muted">Saving changes desired configuration; it does not prove that a workbench has received it or stopped.
        Execution readiness remains unavailable.</p>
</section>
